blocks.en:
We derive 10 categories from professional motion-design websites, award categories, template libraries, and creative portfolios [ 25 , 5 , 7 ] :
(1) Explainer Motion Graphics; (2) Branding & Promotional Motion;
(3) Kinetic Typography; (4) UI & Product Motion;
(5) Data & Infographic Animation; (6) Title Sequences;
(7) Broadcast & Show Graphics; (8) Illustrative & Character Narrative;
(9) Abstract & Experimental Motion; and (10) 3D Motion.
The categories are further refined into 24 subtypes using YouTube [ 61 ] examples, considering communication purpose, visual structure, and temporal organization. This taxonomy supports multiple labels per task and guides data collection and category-level analysis. We further define three complementary complexity dimensions, each with three levels.

